// A tab is ONE column, not a jump to the next tab stop: the compiler cannot
// know the reader's tab width, so it picks the only width it can echo back.
// diag.rs prints the source line with each tab as a single space, which is
// what keeps the caret under the column the message names. The line below is
// indented with one real tab character, so `nope` starts at column 8.
if (true) {
	print(nope);
}
